/-!
# F112-P94D3FO — the COMPLETE noncommutative code-fiber kernel

For every function f : A → B, the kernel of the actual mathlib FreeGroup.map f
is EXACTLY the normal closure of ALL two-letter differences of source letters
whose f-images agree. Neither nonemptiness of A nor surjectivity of f is assumed.
The reverse inclusion is proved using the universal property of the free group:
a receiver constant on f-fibers extends to target letters, choosing identity
outside the image. Applying this to the normal-closure quotient detects every
kernel element, without choosing any nonexistent preimage.

Specialize this generic theorem to the EXISTING full dependent original 18D
DV code transport. This closes the complete-kernel normal-generation obligation,
not merely the existence of one nontrivial FJ two-letter element. It also gives
an exact receiver-descent iff: every complete source-code collision must have
equal receiver images. Extension to the entire target free group is an existence
statement, not uniqueness outside the image of the code function.

Old FJ physical nonempty contexts give NONTRIVIAL normal closures; the separate
FK/FL/FM constructor-preserving presentation gives the TRIVIAL closure at every
finite context. The different source/target alphabets are kept distinct.

This is an algebraic normal presentation indexed by ALL actual code collisions.
It does NOT show the known single FJ defect normally generates the kernel, nor
supply a finite/minimal/computable generating set or a geometric 19D Type filler.
Preserve DS and old no-go, 107 public roots, strict Kuu primary and independent
Kuu as a presentation. No Gray, new axioms, sorry/admit, global strict n-category
or hyperdescent claim. Apache-2.0. Copyright Hidetoshi Itakura / 板倉英俊.
-/

